Fix critical _do_add bug, add test dataset, improve website search

Critical bug fix:
- aggregator.py _do_add() was missing 'return True' -- every ADD was
  treated as energy-rejected (returned None/falsy). This caused 0 merges
  in ALL previous runs, inflating the DB from ~10-15k to 32k entries.
  Test run: 0 ADDs -> 492 ADDs with the fix.

Test infrastructure:
- scripts/build_test_dataset.py: Builds a curated ~2000 food test set
  from known problem cases (banana/dried, rice/cooked, brand names)
  plus Foundation/SR anchors and random diversity sample
- aggregate.py test mode now uses tests/test_fooddata.csv instead of
  first 1000 items from fooddata.csv (which were mostly alcohols)
- Test output goes to tests/test_aggregated.json (separate from prod)

Website search improvements (docs/index.html):
- Prefix matching: chedd now finds Cheddar Cheese (was exact-only)
- Source name search: nutella finds Hazelnut Spread via reverse index
- Binary search on sorted token keys for efficient prefix lookup
